cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research software or its analysis, please cite this repository
  and record the commit used. Cite the related publications separately when
  discussing their methods or findings.
type: software
title: "Prompt-injection fine-tuning on one 16 GB GPU: nine ineligible checkpoints"
authors:
  - given-names: Yaroslav
    family-names: Bondar
    website: "https://github.com/bonyaroslav"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bonyaroslav/aar-prompt-injection-16gb-gpu"
url: "https://github.com/bonyaroslav/aar-prompt-injection-16gb-gpu"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-13
abstract: >-
  Research software, protocols, and numeric results for one response-only QLoRA
  recipe on Qwen3.5-2B using an RTX 4080 with 16 GB GPU memory. Three runs produced
  nine checkpoints; none met the preset capability requirements. The included
  analysis package recalculates visible scores and acceptance decisions without
  model weights or a GPU. Historical generated outputs were not retained.
  The local study adapts an evaluation setting from automated alignment research
  and uses SecFid to frame limitations of attack-success measurements.
keywords:
  - prompt-injection
  - llm-evaluation
  - llm-security
  - fine-tuning
  - qlora
  - local-llm
  - qwen
  - negative-results
